## Claim 4 — Corrected

> The italic type cut for that series was designed by Aldus himself.

**Correction:** The italic introduced for Aldus Manutius’s octavo classical series—first used for the April 1501 Virgil—was designed and cut by Aldus’s punchcutter Francesco Griffo da Bologna, working from contemporary Italian chancery/humanistic cursive. Aldus commissioned, financed, published, and sought privileges for the type; he did not design it himself.

