## Claim 14 — Corrected

> The Hypnerotomachia Poliphili's dense mixture of languages keeps its readership confined to specialists who can meet it in the original.

**Correction:** English rendering/discussion as 'The Dream of Poliphilo' has circulated since at least 1951, so readership is not confined to specialists meeting the polyglot original in the original languages. Although the original's macaronic Italian is notoriously difficult, the work has circulated in translation since 1546 and its French reception reached architects and artists, so its readership is not confined to specialists able to read the original.

